Damn short actually. Try looking at asscention posts.

1. Ditch some arrows. Are you still basic in it? Keep the + arrows in a
stash. You want to collect them to use where you're at *least* skilled.
2. Lower your weight until you're not burdened. I have no idea
what *else* you may be carrying, but you need to carry the least
possible. Swapping crystal plate for splint or banded may seem silly,
but the weight penalty will kill you easily. With only 46 HP, surviving
the mines down to minetown could be tricky otherwise. Absolutely going
much lower could be too, but your AC is good to *get* to the last door
in sokoban. You need something to be able to stay alive *after* you
open it. That means normal or increased speed, strength (either permanently),
or a *real* good weapon you're not unskilled in. That is an artifact
if one comes along. More HP would help, but not near as much as you
might think. Certainly less than 150 wouldn't make a lot of difference.
It's mostly in your own attacks and weapon ability. BTW you *should* be
best in bow right now and *maybe* skilled in dagger. Start collecting them
into piles of about 20 and stashing them now. You'll want them later.

I gather from the status line that you didn't even go in the mines? I
generally do just to see if there's any tools (or food) there and see
what shops are there for what I can't buy right off. It is tough to
survive if you're not paranoid - a definite disadvantage with nethack.
Really. By the time you get to sokoban you will want a key/credit
card/lockpick, a blindfold/towel, a pickaxe/mattock (although I wouldn't
carry a mattock if I were you. I'd sooner kill a peaceful dwarf for a
pickaxe). 



